}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0107",
  "reason": "Check laptop online state, disk space, and warnings for Teams camera black screen and mic issue"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry about the Teams trouble. Please try these steps first: in Teams, go to Settings, then Devices, and confirm the correct microphone, speaker, and camera are selected. Check that the laptop's mute key and camera privacy shutter aren't blocking anything, and close other apps that might be using the camera, such as Zoom or a browser tab with a video call. Then fully quit Teams (right-click its taskbar icon and choose Quit), reopen it, and use Make a test call. If you use a headset or dock, unplug and replug it. Please reply and tell us whether the camera works after these steps, whether the problem happens on every call even after a restart, and whether you're using BL-LT-0107 or a different computer. If it still isn't working, we'll escalate it to a senior technician.",
  "internal_note": "User Sofia Rossi (ID 7, Marketing, America/New_York), account active, not blocked, no failed logins. Assigned device BL-LT-0107 (Windows 11) shows offline with no check-in for 12 days, so the reporter may be on another machine or the laptop may not be connecting. Camera detection by Windows is unknown. Followed KB-025 quick checks and fix steps by sending them to the user. Escalation criteria in KB-025 (recurring after restart, or camera not detected by Windows) are not yet confirmed. Next: get the user's answers on the device in use, whether Windows detects the camera, and whether the issue persists after restart. Escalate if the criteria are met. No action tools were used.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-025"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
